description:
Identify and model the structured SRD data needed for complete level-1 D&D character creation. The generated rules pack is necessary but may not be sufficient if required choices are only stored as prose.

Candidate metadata
- class skill choice sets;
- starting equipment choices;
- spellcasting choice counts;
- class spell lists by level;
- ancestry ability bonuses and traits;
- background proficiencies and equipment;
- languages;
- tool proficiencies;
- armor/weapon proficiencies;
- features granted at level 1;
- formulas or metadata for derived values.

Design rule
The CLI should not parse prose to discover core mechanical choices. If a required character creation choice is only represented as prose, add importer/schema support or a deterministic derived metadata layer.

Acceptance criteria
- Inventory which required level-1 choices are already structured in the generated pack and which are prose-only/missing.
- Add or propose schema/importer changes for missing required choice metadata.
- Character creation engine can enumerate pending required choices for at least one martial class and one spellcasting class.
- Any remaining incompleteness is explicitly tracked in child beads rather than hidden in the CLI.
